 "prediction_scored": "hit: IRR per 5 C 4.09 (3.76 to 4.45) lies in the registered 1.5-5 range; RR at the 95th percentile (33.3 C) vs the median (26.7 C) is 11.2, above 3 as predicted. The registered yearly secondary was weak: Spearman rho of yearly SPARCS heat ED visits with days >= 90 F was 0.36 (p 0.15, 17 years); with days >= 95 F (not registered) it was 0.84.",
 "settle": "The daily relation is settled. Its size relative to the literature is not comparable as published: the NYC syndromic series counts chief-complaint matches and is near zero on mild days, whereas Sun 2021 used claims diagnoses and a contrast of the local 95th percentile against a cooler reference day (not the median, as the registration assumed). A daily SPARCS series of heat-illness ED visits by NYC neighbourhood (not public) would settle the size and allow the neighbourhood analysis that the bridge needs.",
